subproblems.statement:
Let P, n ∈ ℕ, U ⊆ ℝ^P arbitrary, and let R = (M, θ, ξ) be an integer multiplicity triple of dimension n in U (IMRep U n). That is:
- M = R.carrier;
- ξ = R.orient : ℝ^P → Λ_n(ℝ^P) = MultiVector P n is AEStronglyMeasurable for ν := Hⁿ⌞M = μHE[n].restrict M;
- for ν-a.e. x there is a subspace Q with HasApproximateTangentSpaceAt n M x Q and IsUnitOrientationOf (ξ x) Q.
For x ∈ ℝ^P let T_x := approxTangentPlane n M x: the chosen approximate tangent n-plane of M at x when one exists (it is then unique), and {0} otherwise. Let p_x := T_x.starProjection, the orthogonal projection onto T_x, viewed in L(ℝ^P, ℝ^P) with the operator-norm topology. Then x ↦ p_x is almost-everywhere strongly measurable (AEStronglyMeasurable) with respect to ν.
